    Keep unverified historical closures visible and collector crash-free
    
    The Act 19 candidate crashed on the live state root: addendum records are
    stored beside case objects and one is a top-level JSON list, so read() returns
    a list and reconcile() dies on case.get(), leaving index.json stale. The
    canonical dirty checkout already carried this guard but no durable branch did.
    
    Add the isinstance guard, filter index inputs to real case objects, and record
    closed cases that have no case-bound closure artifact under
    unresolved_without_closure_evidence. This does not reopen or rewrite any case
    object and does not change open-case dispatch: it makes obligations that were
    hidden by an evidence-less verified_closed label visible to monitoring, as
    Act 23 §5.1/§7 require. Cases with an artifact present stay unlisted.
    
    Tested on a copy of the live institutional-cases directory: reconcile exits 0
    and lists the four continuity cases plus five other evidence-less closures.

